## Metadata
Title: FUN's Cross-Word Puzzle
Author: H. J. Stack
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-06-14
Number: 23
Description: An X of two stepped bands, 28 rows by 21 columns: one band runs from a single square at the top right (r1c16) down to ONE at the bottom left, the other from ROB (r15) down to FINISH at the bottom right, with PLANT jutting out to the left edge at r18; they cross at EQUAL, URN and BANKER (r21-r23). Squares outside the bands are shown as _.
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-06-14, p. 87
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-06-21, p. 86


